BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 344.00 Td (Vertical Scaling is the process of increasing the power/capacity \(CPU, RAM, storage\) of one server. In the) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 330.60 Td (context of database it is about making one database machine more powerful instead of adding more machines.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 310.70 Td (Instead of adding more servers, you:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 290.80 Td (Increase CPU) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 270.90 Td (Add more RAM) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 251.00 Td (Upgrade storage \(faster disks / more capacity\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 231.10 Td (Improve network bandwidth) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 211.20 Td (It\222s a quick and easy solution when you have a smaller database. \(considering that in today\222s day and age our) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 197.80 Td (infra is on cloud and we dont have to deal with the all the ugliness that comes with it, as the cloud providers) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 184.40 Td (provide us with one click solution to upgrade the database while they handle all the complexities \)) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 58.00 153.50 Td (Challenges in Vertical Scaling) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 135.85 Td (Hard ceiling / physical hardware limit) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 115.95 Td (There\222s always a maximum size for a machine. At some point, you hit the largest instance your cloud provider) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 102.55 Td (offers \(or the biggest box you can reasonably buy\). After that, you have to think about horizontal scaling.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 82.65 Td (Potential downtime during upgrades) Tj ET
