BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 778.00 Td (Scaling up often requires a reboot or some kind of failover:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 758.10 Td (On many setups, the database has to restart on a bigger machine.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 738.20 Td (Managed services \(like AWS RDS, Cloud SQL, etc.\) automate this, but you still often see a short hiccup where) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 724.80 Td (connections drop or error out for a few seconds.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 704.90 Td (For users, this can look like a brief period where the app feels slow or returns errors.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 685.00 Td (Single point of failure) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 665.10 Td (All your workload is concentrated on one main server. If that machine:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 645.20 Td (Has a hardware issue,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 625.30 Td (Crashes, or) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 605.40 Td (Needs emergency maintenance,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 585.50 Td (your database can go down until it\222s fixed or a backup takes over.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 565.60 Td (Cost grows non-linearly) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 545.70 Td (Bigger instances are often much more expensive than smaller ones. At some point, it can be cheaper \(and more) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 532.30 Td (scalable\) to add more machines \(horizontal scaling\) instead of endlessly upgrading a single monster server.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 58.00 499.40 Td (What is Horizontal Scaling?) Tj ET
