BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 514.92 Td (When a write comes to the API:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 495.02 Td (The API sends the write to the primary.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 475.12 Td (The primary sends the change to the replica\(s\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 455.22 Td (The write is considered successful only after the replica\(s\) confirm the update.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 435.32 Td (The API will not respond \223OK\224 until both primary and replica have written the data.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 415.42 Td (Pros:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 395.52 Td (Very strong consistency \226 replicas are always up to date.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 375.62 Td (Replication lag ~= 0 \(no measurable delay between primary and replica\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 355.72 Td (Cons:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 335.82 Td (Slower writes \(you\222re effectively writing to multiple databases on every request\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 315.92 Td (If a replica is slow or down, it can affect write latency/availability.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 58.00 285.02 Td (2. Asynchronous replication) Tj ET
