BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 462.23 Td (This is what most production systems use by default.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 442.33 Td (The primary commits the write and immediately acknowledges success to the API.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 422.43 Td (Replicas pull changes from the primary later \(via logs, binlog, WAL, etc.\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 402.53 Td (The replica applies those changes on its own copy of the data.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 382.63 Td (Pros:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 362.73 Td (Writes are fast \226 you only block on the primary.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 342.83 Td (System is more available even if a replica is slow.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 322.93 Td (Cons:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 303.03 Td (There is replication lag \226 a short window where:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 283.13 Td (The primary has the new value.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 263.23 Td (The replica still has the old value.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 243.33 Td (Reads from replicas may see slightly stale data.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 223.43 Td (This is the trade-off: strong consistency vs. performance and availability.) Tj ET
