BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 498.90 Td (When you shard a database, the shard key decides how your data and traffic are split across machines. When) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 485.50 Td (you shard/partition data, you expect traffic to be spread out evenly.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 465.60 Td (A shard that receives disproportionately high traffic \(reads or writes\) compared to others, then it becomes a) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 452.20 Td (bottleneck while other shards sit mostly idle. This is called as hot partiotion. Example:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 432.30 Td (You shard by country) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 412.40 Td (60% of users are from US) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 392.50 Td (The US shard is overloaded = hot) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 372.60 Td (Other shards \(for smaller countries\) are mostly idle = cold) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 352.70 Td (In that case, even if you have 10 shards, your system behaves like one overloaded shard.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 332.80 Td (So a good shard key should have:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 312.90 Td (High Cardinality) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 293.00 Td (High cardinality makes it easier to avoid hot partitions, because the key space is nicely spread out.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 273.10 Td (Good: user_id, order_id, tenant_id) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 253.20 Td (Bad: country, plan_type, created_at \(only a few values -> some shards get all traffic\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 233.30 Td (Align with Query Patterns) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 213.40 Td (Your shard key should match how your application queries data.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 193.50 Td (If most queries are WHERE user_id = ? -> shard by user_id) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 173.60 Td (If you usually load \223all data for a user\224 -> that user\222s data should live on one shard) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 153.70 Td (If your shard key has nothing to do with your query filters, you\222ll end up with:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 133.80 Td (Cross-shard queries) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 113.90 Td (Distributed joins) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 94.00 Td (Higher latency and complexity) Tj ET
