BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 344.00 Td (There can be a scenario when there are millions of entries in the WAL which can impact the restart time of a) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 330.60 Td (node. This is addressed by taking snapshots of the database at regular intervals. On restart after a failure, only) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 317.20 Td (the WAL entries that were appended after the last snapshot are executed. This greatly reduces the number of) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 303.80 Td (WAL entries that need to be executed to reconstruct the prior state of the database and hence improves the) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 290.40 Td (performance.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 58.00 259.50 Td (2. Consistency) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 241.85 Td (Consistency in the context of ACID transactions ensures that any transaction will bring the database from one) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 228.45 Td (valid state to another valid state never leaving it in a broken or \223invalid\224 state.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 208.55 Td (By Consistency, we refer to both types :) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 188.65 Td (Consistency in reads) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 168.75 Td (Consistency in Data) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 148.85 Td (Lack of Atomicity and lack of isolation leads to inconsistent data.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 128.95 Td (Consistency means that all data integrity rules are true before and after a transaction. Those rules are things) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 115.55 Td (like:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 95.65 Td (PRIMARY KEY \226 no duplicate IDs) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 75.75 Td (FOREIGN KEY \226 child rows must point to existing parent rows) Tj ET
