BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 778.00 Td (LSNs are used to:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 758.10 Td (Track how far the database has applied WAL to the main data files.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 738.20 Td (Coordinate replication \(e.g., a standby server has replayed up to LSN X\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 718.30 Td (Implement point-in-time recovery \(replay up to a certain LSN and then stop\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 698.40 Td (So you can think of the WAL as a big ordered timeline of changes, and the LSN is your precise timestamp on) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 685.00 Td (that timeline.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 665.10 Td (Thanks for reading LevelYouUp! Subscribe for free to receive new posts and support my work.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 58.00 634.20 Td (7. How This All Ties Back to Commit) Tj ET
q 479.00 0 0 308.69 58.00 302.86 cm /Im44 Do Q
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 293.86 Td (Phase 1: The Active Transaction) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 273.96 Td (Request: You send an UPDATE or INSERT command.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 254.06 Td (Modify Memory \(RAM\): The database locates the specific data page in its Buffer Pool \(RAM\) and modifies it right) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 240.66 Td (there.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 220.76 Td (Status: This page is now marked as a \223Dirty Page\224 because the version in RAM is newer than the version on) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 207.36 Td (the hard drive.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 187.46 Td (Generate Log: Simultaneously, the database creates a WAL record describing this change \(including the LSN -) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 174.06 Td (Log Sequence Number\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 154.16 Td (Phase 2: The Commit \(Durability\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 134.26 Td (Request: You call COMMIT.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 114.36 Td (Prepare WAL: The database calculates the CRC-32 \(checksum\) for the log records.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 94.46 Td (Flush WAL to Disk: It forces only the WAL records \(up to the current LSN\) to be written physically to the disk.) Tj ET
