BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 778.00 Td (Note: The main data file on the disk is still old. The new data exists only in the WAL \(on disk\) and the Dirty Page) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 764.60 Td (\(in RAM\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 744.70 Td (Acknowledge: The database tells you: \223Commit successful.\224) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 724.80 Td (Phase 3: The Background Checkpoint \(The \223Dirty Page\224 Flush\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 704.90 Td (This happens asynchronously, minutes later, or when the log gets too big.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 685.00 Td (Identify: The Checkpoint process looks at the Buffer Pool for \223Dirty Pages\224 \(pages modified in RAM but not yet) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 671.60 Td (on disk\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 651.70 Td (Flush Data: It writes these Dirty Pages from RAM directly to the Main Table/Index Files on the disk.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 631.80 Td (Sync: It ensures these data file writes are physically synced to the hardware.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 611.90 Td (Truncate Log: It marks the WAL segments prior to this checkpoint as \223recyclable\224 or \223ready for archive,\224) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 598.50 Td (because that data is now safely inside the main data files.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 578.60 Td (Phase 4: Crash Recovery \(If the plug is pulled\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 558.70 Td (Scenario: The power failed after Phase 2 \(Commit\) but before Phase 3 \(Checkpoint\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 538.80 Td (Restart: The database engine boots up.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 518.90 Td (Locate Checkpoint: It reads and finds the LSN of the last successful checkpoint.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 499.00 Td (Logic: \223Everything before this LSN is guaranteed to be in the data files. I can ignore it.\224) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 479.10 Td (Scan Forward: It reads the WAL files starting from that Checkpoint LSN up to the end of the log.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 459.20 Td (Verify: It checks the CRC-32 of the log entries to ensure the crash didn\222t corrupt the last half-written log line.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 439.30 Td (Redo \(The Replay\):) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 419.40 Td (It sees a committed transaction in the WAL.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 399.50 Td (It checks the data page. The page has an older LSN \(because the RAM was wiped out\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 379.60 Td (It applies the change from the WAL to the page to restore the data.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 359.70 Td (Undo \(The Rollback\):) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 339.80 Td (It sees a transaction in the WAL that started but has no \223COMMIT\224 record.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 319.90 Td (It discards those changes to ensure consistency.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 300.00 Td (I know this article felt like too much words, and less visuals. But the topic is such, i had to cover everything that) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 286.60 Td (happens behind the scenes. But hope you got a fair understanding of WAL and how databases manage the) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 273.20 Td (heavy lifting for us behind the scenes. If you want more such powerful and extremely informative content right to) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 259.80 Td (your inbox, then please do follow and subscribe.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 239.90 Td (Thanks for reading LevelYouUp! Subscribe for free to receive new posts and support my work.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 220.00 Td (Thanks for reading LevelYouUp! This post is public so feel free to share it.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 200.10 Td (Share) Tj ET
